Z||000000||bcwawright||05-15-2001||10:46 AM||||Anyone used these conversion kit?<BR>How did it work...is it worth the money?<BR>Any problems.....especially with rotors warping or cracking?<BR>Any chatter(hehe)<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Spyder replica||||reg||5
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||05-15-2001||11:23 AM||||I looked into the Movit Kit , but at $2700 for a front kit only it's not worth it. We have big reds on our 94 911RSR and there expensive for pads , and rotor replacement. I decided to go with 11.25" rotos with wilwood 4 piston calipers upfront and 11.25" discs in rear with Cadillac calipers. about $800 US to do this conversion. I got my rotors Cryo treated to disapate heat better. The major factor i looked at is that I use my car for track events and I want parts replacement to be cheap.<P>From what I have heard from other racers that have done the 11.25" conversion, they can stop on par with any c2 non turbo 911 (no big reds) c4/c5 vettes. The convesion also uses the factory brake bias setup. So everything feels stock but pedal feel is 10000 times better and far more controlled than the usual fiero on/off brake feel. Plus stopping distances are greatly reduced..<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bcwawright||05-15-2001||11:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>I looked into the Movit Kit , but at $2700 for a front kit only it's not worth it. We have big reds on our 94 911RSR and there expensive for pads , and rotor replacement. I decided to go with 11.25" rotos with wilwood 4 piston calipers upfront and 11.25" discs in rear with Cadillac calipers. about $800 US to do this conversion. I got my rotors Cryo treated to disapate heat better. The major factor i looked at is that I use my car for track events and I want parts replacement to be cheap.<P>From what I have heard from other racers that have done the 11.25" conversion, they can stop on par with any c2 non turbo 911 (no big reds) c4/c5 vettes. The convesion also uses the factory brake bias setup. So everything feels stock but pedal feel is 10000 times better and far more controlled than the usual fiero on/off brake feel. Plus stopping distances are greatly reduced..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks Jonathan<BR>You jusy saved my marriage....I owe you a big mac with fries and a beer(oops! I mean Coke)<P>||||reg||1
